questions.stem:
A vending machine tracks coins per row with this fragment:
int[] coins = {4, 9, 2, 7};
int total = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < coins.length; i += 2) { total += coins[i]; }
System.out.println(total);
What value is printed?

A weather station program crashes at run time on this code:
int[] temps = new int[5];
for (int i = 0; i <= temps.length; i++) { temps[i] = i * 2; }
Which statement identifies the fault?

A dice club audits its rolls with this fragment:
int[] rolls = {2, 5, 2, 6, 2, 1};
int count = 0;
for (int r : rolls) { if (r == 2) { count++; } }
System.out.println(count);
What value is printed?

A scoreboard operator displays finals in reverse with this loop over int[] nums = {10, 20, 30, 40};:
for (int i = nums.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) { System.out.print(nums[i] + " "); }
What line of output appears?

A lifeguard program must finish a routine that finds the tallest wave:
int best = nums[0];
for (int i = 1; i < nums.length; i++) {
  _____
}
Which missing line completes it correctly?

A quiz app totals five scores and must divide by the count:
int sum = 0;
for (int n : nums) { sum += n; }
double avg = sum / (double) _____;
Which fragment finishes the average computation?

A ticket kiosk weights each fare by its position with this fragment:
int[] a = {5, 1, 4};
int t = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) { t += a[i] * i; }
System.out.println(t);
What integer is printed?

A bus depot edits its stop list with this fragment:
ArrayList<String> stops = new ArrayList<>();
stops.add("elm");
stops.add("oak");
stops.set(0, "pine");
System.out.println(stops.get(0) + "-" + stops.size());
What is printed?

A print queue holds numbers with this fragment:
ArrayList<Integer> line = new ArrayList<>();
line.add(10); line.add(20); line.add(30); line.add(40);
line.remove(1);
Which statements about the list afterward are true? Select all that apply.

A volunteer roster fails to compile on this code:
ArrayList<String> names = new ArrayList<>();
names.add("ana");
String s = names[0];
Which statement identifies the fault?

A library kiosk must print every title from an ArrayList named catalog:
for (int i = 0; _____; i++) { System.out.println(catalog.get(i)); }
Which guard completes the loop safely?

A locker helper searches for tag 19 with this fragment:
int[] lockers = {12, 7, 19, 4};
int target = 19, where = -1;
for (int i = 0; i < lockers.length; i++) { if (lockers[i] == target) { where = i; } }
System.out.println(where);
What is printed?

A warehouse robot binary-searches shelf codes with this fragment:
int[] data = {3, 8, 12, 17, 23, 31};
int lo = 0, hi = 5, target = 17, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { steps++; int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; if (data[mid] == target) { break; } else if (data[mid] < target) { lo = mid + 1; } else { hi = mid - 1; } }
System.out.println(steps);
How many loop iterations run?

A phone book routine narrows its window with this fragment:
while (lo <= hi) {
  int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;
  if (data[mid] == target) { return mid; }
  else if (data[mid] < target) { _____; }
  else { hi = mid - 1; }
}
Which line belongs in the blank?

A card player inserts each new card with this fragment:
for (int i = 1; i < a.length; i++) {
  int key = a[i];
  int j = i - 1;
  while (_____) { a[j + 1] = a[j]; j--; }
  a[j + 1] = key;
}
Which guard belongs in the blank?

A timing board crashes inside this bubble sort:
for (int i = 0; i < scores.length; i++) {
  for (int j = 0; j <= scores.length - 1; j++) {
    if (scores[j] > scores[j + 1]) { int t = scores[j]; scores[j] = scores[j + 1]; scores[j + 1] = t; }
  }
}
Which statement identifies the fault?

A librarian audits shelf pairs with this fragment:
int c = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) { for (int j = i; j < 4; j++) { c++; } }
System.out.println(c);
What integer is printed?
